ut  suddenly  some errors were stable but there was no  way to tell how long stable errors would  last or to predict when stable errors  would occur  this is the three-body problem which the  title of the book refers to  the tricelerians spent eons attempting  to solve the three-body problem but  eventually realized that there was no  solution  they needed a new star system  we know that the tricelerians do not  have the ability to lie this is because  their thoughts are displayed openly  instantly readable to other tricelerians  this is why they never developed the  capacity for deception  lying was impossible when your thoughts  were not private  tricelerian mating was also vastly  different from humans  when two tricelerians made it organic  material from both bodies became one  approximately 66 percent of the material  would be used to power the biochemical  reaction which would renew the cells and  create a new body  this new body would then divide into  between three and five new individuals  who would each inherit some of their  parents memories and go on to begin the  cycle again the leader of the  tricelarens is referred to by the title  of princeps essentially the princeps  fills the role that a king or emperor  would fill on earth only on a global  scale  because of the nature of their existence  and the instability of their planet  their culture developed to value only  survival  some tricelerian individuals however saw  the faults in their civilization such as  the listener the lowly triceleran who  first heard the call of earth and  betrayed his species by warning us not  to respond to their message when  explaining to the princess why he had  betrayed his own world he told them that  it was so his own life would not be  wasted  he was too old and too low of status to  mate and try solaris offered nothing to  those on the lower echelons of their  civilization  but by warning earth he could give  humanity a chance to survive listener  compared trisolari